WEBVTT

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:07.040
Sahashi Minato-kun, I presume?

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:09.710
Um... Yes.

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:13.550
That was quite an impressive attack you pulled off.

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:15.050
Attack...?

00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:17.840
Then you're the one from the East?

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:21.760
It's a pleasure to meet you. My name is Higa Izumi.

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:26.180
So... we finally meet.

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:32.230
This is...

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:35.150
The thing you're all looking for.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:39.110
Then... this must be Chiho-san's treatment data...!

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:56.330
atarashii yakusoku ga kokoro wo tsuyoku tsunagu

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:56.330
Our new promise binds our hearts together strongly

00:00:56.670 --> 00:01:03.420
kawaru sekai ni kane ga hibiku yukou

00:00:56.670 --> 00:01:03.420
The bell rings in the changing world, let's go

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:10.260
owari naki tatakai ga subete wo hiki saitemo

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:10.260
Even if the endless fight shreds everything apart,

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:16.440
kimi no hohoemi tada shinjite

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:16.440
I will believe in your smile

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:20.650
kimi no yume mamoreru nara

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:20.650
If I can protect your dream,

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:24.240
itami sae dakishimeyou

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:24.240
I will even embrace pain

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:33.540
kasane au kono omoi mune no chikai yuzurenai

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:33.540
I can't let go of these piling feelings, this oath in my heart

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:40.290
aa, sora no haruka hate made

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:40.290
Ah, all the way to the end of the sky,

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:48.510
sou, kakete yuku you na kasoku shiteku jounetsu

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:45.090
yes, my passion accelerates

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:48.510
as if it were rushing through my body

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:54.680
aa, donna unmei datte

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:54.680
Ah, no matter what kind of fate awaits me,

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:05.820
sou, takaku koeteku makenai yuuki kureta kara

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:58.980
yes, I can fly high over it

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:05.820
because you gave me this undefeatable courage

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.880
Eleventh Wing:

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.880
Preparations for the Festival

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:19.140
Why did you use Uzume-san?

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:27.300
No. 10 volunteered herself in order to extend the lifespan of her Ashikabi.

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:31.130
All I did was respect her decision.

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:37.040
Moreover, the fact that she ceased to function was an accident, and neither was it my intention.

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:39.370
I find it quite regretful as well.

00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:41.580
Saying something like this won't...!

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:48.250
I don't particularly care about what you think of me, but those girls are M.B.I.'s victims.

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:50.180
What are you saying?

00:02:50.550 --> 00:02:52.880
And so are we, for that matter.

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:56.590
Just think about it.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:04.810
One day, all of a sudden, becoming this thing called Ashikabi and getting dragged into this life-threatening game...

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:09.560
Don't you find it quite irrational?

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:10.980
W-Well...

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:21.490
What's most unforgivable is the fact this game called The Sekirei Project exists entirely for the fun and entertainment of a single man.

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:23.950
Fun and entertainment...

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:25.310
Yes,

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:28.120
it exists for the enjoyment of Minaka Hiroto.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:30.910
This isn't only about you, either.

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:38.820
There are many who had their normal lives ruined while getting pushed around by the superpower known as the M.B.I.

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:41.890
That might be true, but...

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:47.840
Let me tell you this, though... That Ashikabi's illness cannot be treated by modern medical practices.

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:49.310
Huh? But...

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:55.110
The card merely contains the data about a treatment to slow down its progress.

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:56.270
That's just...

00:03:56.270 --> 00:03:57.320
Then Chiho-san will...!

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:04.700
However, if there were someone to surpass modern medicine...

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:09.240
The M.B.I...

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:18.880
If you truly wish to save that Ashikabi, that is your only option.

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:40.790
Oh, Minato?

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:43.860
Mom, it's me.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:45.330
What is it?

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:48.100
I have a favour to ask of you.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:49.250
A favour?

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:52.170
A treatment method for an illness?

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:53.530
Y-Yeah...

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:56.790
I thought you might be able to find one, since you work at the M.B.I.

00:04:56.790 --> 00:05:01.190
It is true that perhaps with the M.B.I.'s technology something could be done...

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:01.920
Then...

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:03.380
But what's this?

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:08.370
A rounin still relying on his parents at this day and age...

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:10.140
How pitiful.

00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:13.240
You promised me, didn't you?

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:17.350
If you're really a man, don't rely on your mom and figure it out on your own.

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:30.540
Thank goodness that Chiho-tan's life is out of danger due to the data we received.

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:31.470
Yeah...

00:05:31.990 --> 00:05:34.890
But it's still too early to relax, though.

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:35.930
For the time being...

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:38.080
A moment's reprieve, huh?

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:40.430
What's wrong, Minato?

00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:41.870
Actually,

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:44.810
there's something I'd like you all to help me with.

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:48.140
I'm thinking about going to the M.B.I.

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:49.310
You what?

00:05:49.310 --> 00:05:50.770
Th-That's...

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:54.640
Hey, Sahashi Minato-kun! How have you been?

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:56.330
Minaka!

00:05:58.230 --> 00:06:00.160
I heard your story.

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:01.690
S-Story?

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:05.660
It would seem you long for my assistance.

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:07.040
I see.

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:08.120
This is Mom's doing.

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:11.590
I'm quite the benevolent person, you see?

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:14.040
And I'd love to help you.

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:16.230
R-Really?

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:18.500
For some reason, the president is being nice.

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:20.420
Oh, please...

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:22.090
That is...!

00:06:23.010 --> 00:06:28.970
Only if you can make it to the top floor of the Capital Tower by tomorrow, using your own strength!

00:06:28.970 --> 00:06:32.890
The top floor? Um, what does that have to do with this?

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:35.390
Then I pray for your good luck!

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:38.700
To think they'd come to us...

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:42.280
This might be...

00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:46.240
a very dangerous situation.

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:52.490
Even more of our little birds have lost their wings by now, correct?

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:56.090
Yeah, about half of them are gone now.

00:06:57.090 --> 00:07:00.080
It seems you're not in a very good mood, Takami-kun.

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:08.750
I didn't adjust Sekirei for this purpose in the first place...

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:12.970
Actually, I thought of something interesting again.

00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:13.430
Hm?

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:16.890
Something interesting, yet nice as well.

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:18.900
Nice?

00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:20.540
You...

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:21.310
Don't tell me...

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:24.530
I sure got some good material here.

00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:28.190
I told you not to tap into other people's calls, didn't I?!

00:07:31.490 --> 00:07:32.410
Oh, damn!

00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:39.830
This will serve as a satisfactory way to end the second act.

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:44.250
It's finally time to near the climax!

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:52.770
This is Minaka Hiroto.

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:57.830
The Ashikabi without a single victory, it's down to your final chance.

00:07:58.340 --> 00:08:02.350
A certain individual will try to reach the Capital Tower tomorrow.

00:08:02.770 --> 00:08:06.410
All those who successfully manage to prevent him from doing so,

00:08:06.410 --> 00:08:13.770
will be exempted from the termination of function, and an amazing prize will await them!

00:08:13.770 --> 00:08:17.730
Even already victorious individuals are encouraged to participate.

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:20.330
A prize he says.

00:08:20.650 --> 00:08:23.080
A rare item finally appears!

00:08:26.510 --> 00:08:28.970
Well, doesn't this look interesting?

00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:31.920
Attacking M.B.I. directly like that...

00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:34.110
Who in the world could it be?

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:34.890
Who knows?

00:08:34.890 --> 00:08:39.850
It must be some arrogant and stuck-up person.

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:42.690
Wh-Why...?

00:08:42.690 --> 00:08:48.440
Considering the events with Kusano-tan and Kagari-tan, this is still within predictable measures...

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:52.160
Don't worry! Whatever happens, I'll blow them away with my fists!

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:53.520
Exactly.

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:56.960
My water won't allow anything to get in the way of my Ashikabi.

00:08:56.960 --> 00:08:59.460
Kuu and the rest will protect you!

00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:00.580
Everyone...

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:13.720
Despite the amount of wins, it seems that pretty much all the Ashikabi will gather around the M.B.I.

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:18.630
Launching a surprise attack against the M.B.I. was probably the North's intention,

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:21.920
but in the end this turned out to be pretty interesting.

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:27.440
A guest is here to see you.

00:09:27.970 --> 00:09:29.360
Let him in.

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:32.790
All right, I understand the contents of your request.

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:36.260
Don't you think it's a little easy of a job for someone like you?

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:37.780
That doesn't matter.

00:09:38.170 --> 00:09:40.410
As long as you pay up.

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:42.580
That's clear to me.

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:47.490
Do you really think it will work out just by using them?

00:09:47.490 --> 00:09:50.440
We should send our Sekirei too, just in case...

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:53.630
There's no reason for us to dirty our hands directly.

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:55.000
I see.

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:57.780
For someone like him, that is.

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:02.560
I've roughly confirmed the route and the main security.

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:06.420
Though, when it comes to the main M.B.I building,

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:12.030
getting to the roof would be basically impossible without disabling the security.

00:10:12.030 --> 00:10:13.100
Then...

00:10:13.100 --> 00:10:14.650
Are you too...?

00:10:14.650 --> 00:10:20.130
Indeed... Since I have to get into the tower and investigate it properly...

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:23.550
Wh-Why do you look so happy?

00:10:23.550 --> 00:10:26.000
Everyone's moving out then, huh?

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:27.610
Let's do this together!

00:10:27.610 --> 00:10:28.920
Are you all right with that, Minato?

00:10:40.560 --> 00:10:42.930
Come on! It's the night before the big day!

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:47.900
This is the night right before the showdown... Should we really be taking a bath like this?

00:10:47.900 --> 00:10:50.220
This is not just any bath.

00:10:50.220 --> 00:10:52.140
This is the great gathering of Sekirei!

00:10:52.140 --> 00:10:54.990
Gotta blow away the stress before a fight, right?

00:10:54.990 --> 00:10:57.790
Why are you drinking alcohol in the bath, anyway?

00:10:57.790 --> 00:11:00.830
Oh? But this is sacred wine.

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:07.640
Well, rather than madly stressing out, relaxing like this might be just fine.

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:09.450
Just fine!

00:11:09.450 --> 00:11:14.880
This... is the place where I fought Uzume-san for the first time.

00:11:19.380 --> 00:11:21.680
That's why I'll raise my spirits here!

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:25.100
I'm with you there, Musubi!

00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:31.040
I-It's quite lively, isn't it?

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:32.360
Sahashi-san.

00:11:32.360 --> 00:11:35.270
No! It's not like I want to go check it out or anything!

00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:38.070
I'll have a feast ready for tomorrow.

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:43.370
I'll add it to your rent if it all goes to waste.

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:45.290
Landlady...

00:11:45.290 --> 00:11:48.210
Please, be sure to come back.

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:51.170
I understand.

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:55.680
It's not like I don't care about it, either...

00:11:55.680 --> 00:12:00.610
That's why I told Minato to try to come here and get it,

00:12:00.610 --> 00:12:03.870
but that idiot tapped into my call, and it all turned into this.

00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:07.150
I see.

00:12:07.150 --> 00:12:10.100
One thing after another... I'm really sorry.

00:12:10.100 --> 00:12:11.430
It's okay.

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:14.320
This is something Sahashi decided in the first place.

00:12:15.010 --> 00:12:16.110
I...

00:12:16.770 --> 00:12:19.530
We want to grant him his wish.

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:22.400
That's all there is to it.

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:28.890
What a great day for an attack.

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:29.830
It sure is.

00:12:33.530 --> 00:12:35.460
It's been a long time since I got to go outside.

00:12:39.680 --> 00:12:43.120
After seeing Uzume-san and the other Sekirei, I feel that I've finally understood a bit...

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:45.390
Why it's not logical...

00:12:45.730 --> 00:12:48.010
What it means to think and to be thought of...

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:51.100
And about the existence of the precious bonds.

00:12:51.100 --> 00:12:57.170
To protect these bonds, they always give it their best.
There are also times when you have to fight for their sake.

00:12:57.690 --> 00:13:01.280
That's what everyone taught me.

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:04.870
All right, let's go!

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:07.750
How should I say it... Sahashi...

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:09.350
The air around him has changed.

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:12.260
Sekirei are birds who teach love.

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:16.660
They teach about love and get taught about it in return,

00:13:16.660 --> 00:13:19.790
while giving birth to this amazing power called bonds.

00:13:20.140 --> 00:13:22.050
And bringing forth miracles.

00:13:23.040 --> 00:13:25.760
That is why Sekirei were born.

00:13:26.630 --> 00:13:27.760
Miracles...

00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:33.630
Oh, never mind. I just remembered someone mentioning that before.

00:13:34.730 --> 00:13:37.020
Are you ready, Minato-san?

00:13:37.020 --> 00:13:40.810
Don't you think going in broad daylight is a little too bold?

00:13:40.810 --> 00:13:46.470
Not at all. Going during the day - when lots of people are out -
should prevent the M.B.I. from making any big moves...

00:13:47.920 --> 00:13:49.920
This is the M.B.I.

00:13:49.920 --> 00:13:53.810
A Capital-wide decree has been issued for the day.

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:56.420
Please refrain from leaving your homes without permission.

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:58.210
This is the M.B.I.

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:01.160
The president sure knows how to go overboard, doesn't he?

00:14:01.790 --> 00:14:05.340
E-Either way, let's grit our teeth and fight our way through!

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:08.010
Y-Yeah, you're right.

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:10.970
Well then, we'll be going.

00:14:11.060 --> 00:14:14.140
All right, let's roll out!

00:14:14.520 --> 00:14:16.190
We're off, Landlady.

00:14:16.420 --> 00:14:18.360
We're off, Landlady.

00:14:18.360 --> 00:14:20.070
We're off!

00:14:20.070 --> 00:14:22.260
Landlady, we're heading out.

00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:24.530
I'm counting on you to prepare a big party.

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:29.620
Please, be careful and good luck.

00:14:30.730 --> 00:14:34.430
Mina-tan, you'll be on standby near the tower until we contact you.

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:38.420
Musubi-tan, Tsukiumi-tan, and Kazehana-tan will guard Mina-tan.

00:14:38.420 --> 00:14:42.880
We'll get you to the front entrance,
while we will get in through the back.

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:46.300
We will break into the M.B.I.'s server room.

00:14:47.420 --> 00:14:50.760
Is that your idea of disguise...?

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:55.680
Kusano-tan, there's a road which leads to the M.B.I. here, right?

00:14:55.680 --> 00:15:00.640
Yeah, I used to take a walk here with Takami-chan a lot.

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:02.100
But...

00:15:02.720 --> 00:15:05.220
Then a mean person came and...

00:15:08.620 --> 00:15:12.250
That's how she became "The Green Girl," huh?

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:17.470
Well either way, this makes our plan easier.

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:21.470
Over there!

00:15:22.910 --> 00:15:24.660
It's pretty defenceless, isn't it?

00:15:25.030 --> 00:15:28.180
Well, it's just a facility for the botanical garden, after all.

00:15:28.180 --> 00:15:31.760
They can't put up too many guards around here.

00:15:45.860 --> 00:15:50.080
Who would have thought they'd try to get in here... They really don't understand their position.

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:51.190
But...

00:15:51.190 --> 00:15:53.830
this makes things easier.

00:15:54.780 --> 00:15:56.410
It looks like they're here.

00:15:57.540 --> 00:16:00.170
I'll do my best for you, Natsu!

00:16:00.170 --> 00:16:03.790
All right. Then, good luck everyone.

00:16:04.590 --> 00:16:08.050
Leave it to me! You just take it easy!

00:16:09.290 --> 00:16:11.930
Trying to win over a gay guy... What wasted effort.

00:16:11.930 --> 00:16:13.770
Shut it, Haihane!

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:18.100
All right, I'll beat 'em up good.

00:16:21.990 --> 00:16:24.780
Your Sekirei core is shining brighter than ever.

00:16:24.780 --> 00:16:27.360
Right! I've learned the Bear Paw technique!

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:33.280
Even though Yume's not here, it looks like she'll be able to entertain me a bit.

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:39.790
It's so quiet.

00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:42.510
It sure is strange that there's no one here at this time of day.

00:16:42.510 --> 00:16:43.380
Stop.

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:49.030
It doesn't appear any different than usual.

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:50.390
Y-Yeah.

00:16:50.390 --> 00:16:53.510
I thought at least the M.B.I.'s military would be here or something...

00:16:53.510 --> 00:16:56.270
But, it looks there are some others, though.

00:16:56.270 --> 00:16:57.790
What are you talking about?

00:16:57.790 --> 00:17:00.270
So you're the boss monster, huh?

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:09.660
Oh, there's so many.

00:17:09.660 --> 00:17:11.490
So these are the ones who read the message.

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:14.870
We're already surrounded.

00:17:14.870 --> 00:17:18.090
I see. All we have to do is beat these guys, eh?

00:17:18.440 --> 00:17:21.330
We won't have to leave each other if we do that, right?

00:17:25.170 --> 00:17:27.340
Matsu-san, we're actually-

00:17:27.340 --> 00:17:29.850
Mina-tan, I'm very sorry, but...

00:17:30.660 --> 00:17:32.220
M-Matsu-san?

00:17:32.220 --> 00:17:34.730
So you really did come this way.

00:17:34.730 --> 00:17:37.690
How have you been, Green Girl?

00:17:38.310 --> 00:17:41.270
So you're here as well, Scrapped Number.

00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:44.190
We meet... again.

00:17:44.190 --> 00:17:48.610
Well then, time to defeat you guys to acquire the rare item!

00:17:48.610 --> 00:17:50.060
Get 'em!

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:57.320
Sekirei No. 65, Taki.

00:17:59.150 --> 00:17:59.990
Fog?

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:04.980
No!

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:10.300
Matsu! Now's the time!

00:18:11.240 --> 00:18:12.210
Right!

00:18:14.030 --> 00:18:16.140
Long time no see, 02.

00:18:16.680 --> 00:18:19.100
We meet under difficult circumstances.

00:18:19.970 --> 00:18:22.500
I could say the same thing to you, 05.

00:18:23.190 --> 00:18:25.350
No, Mutsu-tan!

00:18:33.610 --> 00:18:35.980
Mutsu, she'll get away!

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:44.870
Fog with ice powder,

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:48.190
I borrowed a bit of her power.

00:18:48.190 --> 00:18:49.130
What do you think?

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:51.040
Dammit!

00:19:01.930 --> 00:19:03.660
Matsu-san, what's wrong?

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:04.450
Matsu-san.

00:19:04.630 --> 00:19:05.810
Matsu-san!

00:19:06.720 --> 00:19:08.040
It got cut off.

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:11.140
Looks like something happened over there, too.

00:19:11.140 --> 00:19:13.230
I guess we have to push through ourselves, huh?

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:17.140
Then, I'll take them all on!

00:19:17.140 --> 00:19:18.480
You can't, Tsukiumi!

00:19:18.480 --> 00:19:19.340
What?

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:22.620
You can't fight them.

00:19:23.250 --> 00:19:26.770
None of these people want to fight.

00:19:26.770 --> 00:19:30.870
But they have no other choice but to come here in order to avoid being separated...

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:32.540
So...

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:38.650
But you know, even though you say that, they won't let us through just like tha-

00:19:45.590 --> 00:19:49.130
Yo, is this where all the fun's going on?

00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:50.660
Who are you?

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:52.650
We're the ones who found him.

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:54.070
Don't butt in!

00:19:54.070 --> 00:19:54.550
That's right!

00:19:54.550 --> 00:19:56.850
A game is all about first come, first serve, isn't it?

00:19:57.520 --> 00:20:00.900
Okay then! Let's go, my lovelies!

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:01.990
'Kay!

00:20:01.990 --> 00:20:05.020
What's up with this guy? He doesn't seem nervous at all.

00:20:05.020 --> 00:20:07.040
Isn't he just some idiot?

00:20:08.620 --> 00:20:09.990
What?!

00:20:09.990 --> 00:20:12.500
Who's the one who just called me an idiot?!

00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:13.500
You?!

00:20:14.720 --> 00:20:15.670
Was it you?!

00:20:16.460 --> 00:20:17.630
Ashikabi-sama!

00:20:22.050 --> 00:20:24.810
You bastards...

00:20:24.810 --> 00:20:27.320
I'll beat the shit out of you!

00:20:31.020 --> 00:20:32.650
Take that, you little-!

00:20:32.650 --> 00:20:36.280
They are all starting to fight each other...

00:20:36.280 --> 00:20:38.900
Wh-What's going on...?

00:20:39.270 --> 00:20:41.100
Anyway, this is our chance.

00:20:41.100 --> 00:20:44.010
Agreed. Let's take this chance to get to the M.B.I.

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:45.330
Yeah...

00:20:53.690 --> 00:20:54.630
It opened up!

00:21:01.100 --> 00:21:03.320
Huh? Do they have a day off today?

00:21:03.620 --> 00:21:05.770
There's nobody here...

00:21:06.300 --> 00:21:08.330
Musubi, don't let your guard down.

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:09.090
No shit.

00:21:15.110 --> 00:21:17.230
We're locked in.

00:21:19.650 --> 00:21:23.860
Minaka thinks he's playing around with his toys,

00:21:24.570 --> 00:21:28.490
but if you play with them in the wrong way, the toys can break.

00:21:31.280 --> 00:21:33.330
Well, ladies and gentlemen,

00:21:33.820 --> 00:21:36.210
the preparation for the festival is complete.

00:21:38.070 --> 00:21:40.590
Enjoy it to your heart's content!

00:21:47.100 --> 00:21:53.250
unmei nante ne zenbu de kimi shidai

00:21:47.100 --> 00:21:53.250
All kinds of fate depend on you

00:21:54.480 --> 00:22:02.050
tsuiteku doko made mo onaji kimochi wo kakaete

00:21:54.480 --> 00:22:02.050
I'll follow you anywhere carrying the same feelings

00:22:13.010 --> 00:22:19.030
mada dare ni mo hakken sarete inai michi mo tairiku ni sou

00:22:13.010 --> 00:22:19.030
